DOES THIS PROPOSAL DECIDE THE PHANTOM-ZONE PRESSURE SIGNATURE?  DECIDES, WITH QUALIFICATION.  (1) WHAT IT DECIDES CLEANLY: the per-cluster outer Compton shape at theta in [theta_500, 2 theta_500] (median 15.5' to 31') at Planck 143 GHz bin SNR 10.2 (8-12'), 9.3 (12-17'), 7.8 (17-23'), 6.6 (23-31'), with a conservative 2-bin slope error of 0.32 per cluster (a multi-bin fit over the four outer bins reaches ~0.15), i.e. 0.09 pooled over the 12 -> the F1 decision line (steeper than -2 at theta_500, killing the G095 extension) separates at ~2 sigma per cluster and ~6 sigma pooled; the F2 line (flatter than the registered [-(q-1)-0.4, -(q-1)+0.4] band, killing the T_inf-isotherm x gas-envelope reading) at ~1.5 sigma per cluster, ~5 sigma pooled.  The model separation vs the classic beta = 2/3 profile is chi2 ~ 3087 (median combined, common-y0 shape comparison; 12/12 clusters > 25).  The inner profile (theta < theta_M, the r_M crossing at 4.7') is ACT/SO-resolved at central SNR 20 for the 7/12 clusters inside the public ACT band (A1795, A2142, A2255, A2319, RXC1825 are outside it and get Planck-alone inner coverage).  (2) WHAT IT DECIDES ONLY PARTIALLY: (i) the 40x/105x phantom-zone multiples are ratios vs the CLASSIC beta = 2/3, r_c = 0.15 R500 convention -- the physically scored quantities are the absolute convolved per-cluster curves and the slope; (ii) A644 (q = 3.8, the steepest gas envelope) carries only ~2.6x hold-up -- for it the signature is a factor, not two decades; (iii) a profile in the framework band confirms the outer pressure hold-up but the mechanism attribution (phantom vs dust envelope vs active EFE cap) is NOT one measurement: the capped reading would steepen the profile back toward the beta family, so the measurement DISCRIMINATES capped vs uncapped (G108's window) but does not by itself prove the phantom density profile rho = A/r^2; (iv) the amplitude y0 is a consistency test (the ~0.05-dex HSE budget), not a free prediction.  (3) WHO CAN RUN IT: any SZ analyst.  All inputs are public today: Planck HFI 100/143/217/353 GHz 2018 maps and the MILCA/NILC y-maps; ACT DR5/DR6 maps (LAMBDA) and the Coulton et al. 2024 arcminute y-map over ~13,000 deg2; the Planck PSZ2 catalog for neighbour subtraction; X-COP profiles (committed in this repo and public); public tools healpy/NILC/fgbuster and matched-filter codes.  No observing time is requested -- this is a pre-registered analysis proposal whose decision rules (F1/F2, the band windows, the chi2 convention, the common-y0 normalization) are fixed in deepseek_push/TSZ_PROPOSAL.md BEFORE the maps are read.  Runtime: ~2-4 weeks of postdoc-level analysis per survey; the SO numbers scale the same thresholds in uK-arcmin when SO maps become public.

